From 865d84132e16df2ea830dbd3f6f84f587064bd8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:21:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 085/112] Filters: coefficients move per sample across each
 block; the gain compensation too

LPF / HPF cutoff, resonance and morph set once per render block (a knob,
automation, an envelope, an LFO) no longer step every block (zipper): the
12 / 24 dB and drive ladders, the HP ladder and the SVF move every coefficient
setConfig() computes in a straight line from the last block's to this one's,
per sample, for voices and the song's / kits' / audio tracks' filters. A
configuration that doesn't change takes the same loops as before: bit-exact
(tests/filters filter_neutral_test, 648 cases, same hash as without the ramps).

- LP ladders: the precise stages where both ends are below their limit; the
  saturation of either end; a mode change or the drive's oversampling switching
  jumps as before (the coefficients mean something else there).
- The filter gain compensation: a voice moves its oscillators' amplitudes per
  sample (it used to jump them where the filter gain changed); the song's, a
  kit's and an audio track's filters move their output from the last block's
  compensation to this one's (renderLongStereo(..., rampGain)), as the caller
  applies it flat with the post-FX volume.
- One loop for both stereo channels and every stride (not inlined): the
  ramp variants cost 32 KB of code instead of 95 KB.

Zipper, block-set vs per-sample-set, above 2 kHz: LP24 cutoff -60.6 -> -67.5
dBc, drive -40.3 -> -58.7, HP ladder -40.5 -> -83.1, SVF -66.4 -> -112.4,
kit LP24 resonance -60.8 -> -73.1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
